{
  "$comment": [
    "Mystery scoring parity table (ARCHITECTURE §4.13): every row of PRD §4.1.7, both tables, plus invalid, duplicate and out-of-turn actions.",
    "Replayed by Vitest against the engine's mystery plugin (src/engine/rounds/mystery/scoring-fixture.test.ts) and, from SQL-5, by the SQL parity tests that scripts/sql/gen-parity.ts generates.",
    "Guesses name entity ids from content/fixtures/answer-lists/country.json, which the e2e track loads. Picks name an option by role (answer, distractor1 to distractor3) because each side draws its own shuffle: parity compares judged results, never shuffles.",
    "Each step is one round action. expect.verdict is the verdict kind; continue carries the clue now open, whether the four options show, and the roles that come back already guessed. expect.error is a refusal, which consumes nothing: the clue stays where it was.",
    "outcome is the resolved round (null when a row ends mid-round). prdShareRow is the PRD's illustrative row; DESIGN §6.11 owns the shipped glyphs, and the semantic cells are what both sides check.",
    "The table holds no clue text: any four clues will do, and public JSON never carries a clues array (scripts/checks/secret-scan.mjs). Each runner supplies its own placeholders."
  ],
